.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1236 PM PDT Mon Oct 5 2026
(Wednesday through next Sunday)

Ridging persists for the next few days and the Heat Advisory has
been extended to Thursday night for the inland and Bayshore regions.
Temperatures across the inland valleys remain in the middle 90s to
near 105 into Thursday; despite a couple of degrees of cooling on
Thursday, hazardous heat lingers across the region and widespread
Moderate HeatRisk persists in the inland regions. Patches of
HeatRisk linger into Friday across the interior, and the Heat
Advisory may need to be extended if confidence in heat-related
impacts increases.

Towards the latter part of the seven day outlook, uncertainty in the
forecast increases as the ridge starts to break down and a trough
begins to develop along the West Coast. Ensemble model cluster
analysis suggests a split between solutions that bring something
akin to an inside slider to the Great Basin for the upcoming weekend
and those that keep the ridging in play. The inside slider solution
slightly dominates the cluster space at this time, but we will wait
for the model trend to become clearer before committing to a
particular solution.

