.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 306 AM PDT Mon Oct 5 2026

Strong ridging aloft will lead to hot and dry conditions through
Thursday with elevated fire weather conditions across the higher
elevations. Poor to very poor overnight humidity recoveries will
continue across the thermal belts with pushes of offshore flow
each morning. Hazardous heat will continue through Thursday with
major to extreme risks of heat-related illnesses across most
mountain ranges. A pattern change later this week will bring
cooler conditions to the region.

